  "narrative": {
    "intro": "W W Grainger recorded $295M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company received 146,995 awards for a $2K average award size, and obligations are down 17.6% year over year. The General Services Administration accounted for the bulk of buying, obligating $292M. Home Centers is the largest market by NAICS with $293M in obligations. Obligations rose from $198M in FY21 to $358M in FY25, then moved to $295M in FY26. The figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values. Current-year totals are partial because FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are W W Grainger's federal obligations?",
        "body": "W W Grainger's federal obligations are highly concentrated with $292M coming from the General Services Administration. W W Grainger has $295M in total obligations year to date and 146,995 awards, which produces a $2K average award size. Obligations are down 17.6% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do W W Grainger's obligations go by market and agency?",
        "body": "W W Grainger's largest market is Home Centers with $293M in obligations. W W Grainger also has obligations in All Other Miscellaneous Electrical Equipment and Component Manufacturing at $396K and Motor and Generator Manufacturing at $282K. Other significant buying agencies include the Department of Transportation at $909K and the Department of Justice at $427K."
      }
    ]
